  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Predictive Maintenance and Asset Health for a Class I railroad fleet of 20 locomotives and railcars across Line Haul, Yard, Bulk, Intermodal, Hazmat, and General fleets. Stakeholders include the VP Mechanical (health score, failure probability, downtime), Reliability Engineering (component failure mix, RUL, emergency events), and the CFO (parts/labor spend vs maintenance budget, capex tradeoffs).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Fleet health score = AVG(health_score); healthy ~80+ (custom 0-100 composite of vibration, bearing temp, oil pressure)\n- Vibration = vibration_g; >3.0 g sustained indicates bearing or wheel-tread wear\n- Bearing temperature = bearing_temp_celsius; >85 C is hot-bearing alert threshold (industry rule of thumb)\n- 30-day failure probability = failure_probability_pct; >25% triggers proactive shopping\n- Remaining useful life = remaining_useful_life_days; <90 days warrants overhaul scheduling\n- Locomotive MTBF benchmark: world-class fleets aim for 2,000+ operating hours between failures; AI-driven PdM can lift MTBF 3-5x over reactive baselines\n- Emergency event share = emergency_count / event_count; world-class reliability programs hold this <5% with the balance being Preventive + Inspection\n- Maintenance cost ratio = (parts_cost_usd + labor_cost_usd) vs maintenance_budget_usd; track budget variance monthly\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - health_monthly (source: rolling_stock) — dims: reading_date, asset_type, fleet; measures: avg_health_score, avg_vibration, avg_bearing_temp, asset_count, low_health_count, total_oil_pressure_psi, max_vibration_g.\n  - maintenance_cost_monthly (source: sensor_readings) — dims: event_date, asset_type, event_type, failure_component; measures: total_parts_cost, total_labor_cost, total_downtime_hours, event_count, emergency_count, unique_asset_count, max_downtime_hours.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. asset_id, asset_name, failure_probability_pct, remaining_useful_life_days, maintenance_budget_usd, actual_maintenance_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show the monthly trend in fleet average health score over the trailing 12 months by asset type.",
    "Top 10 assets by total downtime hours over the last 90 days.",
    "Which assets have a 30-day failure probability above 25% and less than 90 days of remaining useful life?",
    "How has the share of emergency events versus preventive events trended month-over-month across the fleet?",
    "What is the total parts plus labor spend by failure component for the last quarter, and how does it compare to budget?",
    "Top 10 asset types by average bearing temperature this month — flag any above 85 Celsius.",
    "Show monthly maintenance budget versus actual spend by fleet for the upcoming 6 months."
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest vibration g?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(max_vibration_g) AS max_vibration_g",
        "FROM {fqn}.health_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total oil pressure psi changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(total_oil_pressure_psi) AS total_oil_pressure_psi",
        "FROM {fqn}.health_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique assets?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(unique_asset_count) AS unique_asset_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.maintenance_cost_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does the number of unique events vary by asset type?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT asset_type, MEASURE(event_count) AS event_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.maintenance_cost_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_count DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total bearing temperature celsius over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(bearing_temp_celsius) AS total_bearing_temp_celsius",
        "FROM {fqn}.rolling_stock",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total asset downtime hours over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, SUM(downtime_hours) AS total_downtime_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings",
        "GROUP BY event_date ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average 30-day failure probability 0-100 changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, AVG(failure_probability_pct) AS avg_failure_probability_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.maintenance_events",
        "GROUP BY forecast_month ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
